<article class="env-example" id="B9E930">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/B9E930">Example <span data-tag="B9E930">2.3.4.2</span>.</a> Let $\calC $ be a $(-1)$-category. Using condition $(2)$ of Definition <a href="/tag/FF9854" data-tag="FF9854">2.3.4.1</a>, one shows by induction on $m$ that $\calC $ has at most one $m$-simplex. Consequently, we see that up to isomorphism there are precisely two $(-1)$-categories: $\Delta ^{-1} \simeq \emptyset $ and $\Delta ^0$. </p>
